1
00:01:15,784 --> 00:01:19,121
[8. We Were Eighteen]

2
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:26,414
[Episode 8]

3
00:01:33,795 --> 00:01:35,270
Go on in.

4
00:01:35,270 --> 00:01:36,451
Okay.

5
00:01:37,137 --> 00:01:38,297
Well...

6
00:01:47,474 --> 00:01:49,155
Hey...

7
00:01:52,801 --> 00:01:54,464
Shall we shake hands?

8
00:01:55,061 --> 00:01:56,221
What?

9
00:01:56,221 --> 00:01:57,506
A handshake.

10
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:00,708
Why a handshake?

11
00:02:04,478 --> 00:02:06,361
Since we're dating now?

12
00:02:08,113 --> 00:02:09,823
Just do it.

13
00:02:18,931 --> 00:02:20,709
Nice to meet you.

14
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:24,996
What is this?

15
00:02:28,849 --> 00:02:30,491
I'll head in now.

16
00:02:35,108 --> 00:02:36,659
Don't see her.

17
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:49,164
I said don't see her.

18
00:02:49,164 --> 00:02:50,693
I don't want to.

19
00:02:52,339 --> 00:02:54,117
Don't see Hye Min.

20
00:02:55,451 --> 00:02:56,888
Look, Noh Si Ha.

21
00:02:56,888 --> 00:02:59,096
I clearly rejected you.

22
00:02:59,096 --> 00:03:00,679
I don't like you.

23
00:03:00,679 --> 00:03:02,256
You're not the one.

24
00:03:03,183 --> 00:03:05,602
Then shouldn't I decide what I do next?

25
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:07,396
I hate Hye Min.

26
00:03:07,396 --> 00:03:10,806
Even if it's not me, don't see her.

27
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:17,465
No.

28
00:03:18,699 --> 00:03:20,190
I'm going to see her.

29
00:03:35,674 --> 00:03:38,695
I was going to go say hello.
What brings you here?

30
00:03:38,695 --> 00:03:41,601
Where have you been?

31
00:03:42,848 --> 00:03:45,308
I went to visit my parents.

32
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:47,705
Did something happen?

33
00:03:47,705 --> 00:03:50,293
No. It was nothing special.

34
00:03:51,607 --> 00:03:58,449
Yu Gyeom's mother, has it been over 20 years
since you came to this house?

35
00:03:58,449 --> 00:03:59,747
Yes.

36
00:03:59,747 --> 00:04:01,063
If that's the case...

37
00:04:01,869 --> 00:04:08,203
You shouldn't visit your parents
unless someone has died.

38
00:04:08,203 --> 00:04:13,545
Even if someone dies,
you should think twice about going.

39
00:04:13,545 --> 00:04:14,587
Father.

40
00:04:14,587 --> 00:04:19,294
That's how you truly become
a member of this family.

41
00:04:22,387 --> 00:04:24,402
Father. I'm sorry.

42
00:04:31,488 --> 00:04:33,869
Mom. You're a maid.

43
00:04:33,869 --> 00:04:36,656
You only leave that house when you die.

44
00:04:40,113 --> 00:04:42,334
- Mom.
- What?

45
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:45,160
Yu Gyeom won't wake up.

46
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,214
What?

47
00:04:47,955 --> 00:04:49,790
What's wrong with him?

48
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:52,543
Did something happen while I was away?

49
00:04:52,543 --> 00:04:54,611
Mom, I wasn't here either.

50
00:04:56,608 --> 00:04:58,168
Yu Gyeom.

51
00:04:59,961 --> 00:05:01,258
Yu Gyeom?

52
00:05:04,637 --> 00:05:06,895
My son.

53
00:05:06,895 --> 00:05:09,819
He's burning up with a fever.
What should we do?

54
00:05:10,832 --> 00:05:12,479
You can't.

55
00:05:12,479 --> 00:05:13,688
Let go.

56
00:05:13,688 --> 00:05:14,725
Really.

57
00:05:14,725 --> 00:05:16,858
Seriously, you...

58
00:05:16,858 --> 00:05:19,194
Who are you to stop me from seeing him?

59
00:05:19,862 --> 00:05:22,447
What are you doing here
so early in the morning?

60
00:05:22,447 --> 00:05:25,909
I'm the one your father approved of.

61
00:05:25,909 --> 00:05:29,411
Your almighty father.

62
00:05:31,289 --> 00:05:32,968
Right.

63
00:05:32,968 --> 00:05:38,755
But my almighty father says he doesn't
want you to see Yu Gyeom anymore.

64
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:40,937
So just leave.

65
00:05:40,937 --> 00:05:42,133
Why?

66
00:05:42,133 --> 00:05:43,948
Did your wife ask you that?

67
00:05:43,948 --> 00:05:45,637
Did she beg you to keep me away from her son?

68
00:05:45,637 --> 00:05:49,558
Please don't bring Ji Yeong into this.

69
00:05:49,558 --> 00:05:53,144
It gives me the creeps every time
her name comes out of your mouth.

70
00:05:53,144 --> 00:05:55,155
Look here, Cho Jae Jin.

71
00:05:55,155 --> 00:05:57,253
Get a grip.

72
00:05:57,253 --> 00:05:59,731
People would think I'm your mistress.

73
00:05:59,731 --> 00:06:03,389
I'm the first wife. She's the second.

74
00:06:03,389 --> 00:06:05,156
Don't you know what that means?

75
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:07,951
That's what you and my father decided.

76
00:06:07,951 --> 00:06:09,953
I never agreed to any of it.

77
00:06:09,953 --> 00:06:11,167
What?

78
00:06:12,456 --> 00:06:14,152
It was a one-night mistake.

79
00:06:14,152 --> 00:06:15,348
Who?

80
00:06:15,348 --> 00:06:16,511
Me?

81
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:20,463
Me? Not Lee Ji Yeong, but me?

82
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:21,763
Yes.

83
00:06:21,763 --> 00:06:22,799
You.

84
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:24,883
Stop talking nonsense.

85
00:06:25,469 --> 00:06:27,984
I was your first love.

86
00:06:37,731 --> 00:06:39,060
Jae Jin.

87
00:06:39,060 --> 00:06:41,016
I haven't forgotten a thing.

88
00:06:41,016 --> 00:06:43,778
I remember every inch of your body.

89
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:47,074
And you remember every inch of mine, don't you?

90
00:06:47,074 --> 00:06:49,397
That was over 20 years ago.

91
00:06:50,812 --> 00:06:53,163
You were really something back then.

92
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:55,624
You were so cool at the Olympics.

93
00:06:55,624 --> 00:06:59,605
I was so proud that you were my man.

94
00:07:00,754 --> 00:07:03,389
But look at you now.

95
00:07:03,389 --> 00:07:06,214
How did you become worse than trash?

96
00:07:06,214 --> 00:07:08,136
Is this a family trait?

97
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:10,535
Turning a fine person into a total wreck?

98
00:07:10,535 --> 00:07:12,724
It must be a family trait.

99
00:07:12,724 --> 00:07:15,143
Come to think of it, you're not the only one.

100
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:19,105
Il Hee, Dul Hee, Sam Hee,
and now even Yu Gyeom.

101
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:23,526
I will never let Yu Gyeom end up like that.

102
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:27,568
I would hate for Yu Gyeom to become like you.

103
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:33,012
Don't worry.

104
00:07:33,012 --> 00:07:34,454
He won't end up like me.

105
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:35,763
No.

106
00:07:35,763 --> 00:07:36,790
I think he will.

107
00:07:36,790 --> 00:07:38,667
Even so, it's not your business.

108
00:07:38,667 --> 00:07:40,846
Why is it none of my business? I'm his--

109
00:07:40,846 --> 00:07:42,000
Dad.

110
00:07:43,592 --> 00:07:45,365
Dad, hurry up.

111
00:07:45,365 --> 00:07:46,693
Hurry up.

112
00:07:55,684 --> 00:07:57,876
Your mom left.

113
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:03,400
But why do you have to be so mean?

114
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:04,902
I can't even talk.

115
00:08:04,902 --> 00:08:06,736
Jeez.

116
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:09,823
You should cherish those
who are precious to you.

117
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:13,295
Whether it's your sister or your mom...

118
00:08:13,295 --> 00:08:15,374
You just say whatever...

119
00:08:18,035 --> 00:08:20,285
You just lash out at them.

120
00:08:22,002 --> 00:08:24,205
Do you have anger management issues?

121
00:08:28,717 --> 00:08:30,312
Come out already.

122
00:08:30,312 --> 00:08:34,268
It's my first day off in a while,
and I have to go home with you...

123
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:38,685
I'm just so thrilled I could die.

124
00:08:38,685 --> 00:08:42,313
Come out quickly before I get
so excited that I lose my temper.

125
00:08:42,313 --> 00:08:44,023
Hello, sir.

126
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:45,763
I heard the news.

127
00:08:45,763 --> 00:08:48,445
Thank you so much. Our Dul Hee...

128
00:08:48,445 --> 00:08:49,971
You're Seong Eun, right?

129
00:08:49,971 --> 00:08:51,800
Yes, I am.

130
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:53,575
Nice to meet you.

131
00:08:53,575 --> 00:08:55,596
I have a favor to ask.

132
00:08:55,596 --> 00:08:56,689
Yes?

133
00:08:57,495 --> 00:09:01,429
Empty her bank account completely.

134
00:09:01,429 --> 00:09:05,712
Please find her a studio apartment
far away from this neighborhood.

135
00:09:05,712 --> 00:09:07,262
As soon as possible.

136
00:09:07,262 --> 00:09:08,463
Okay?

137
00:09:09,675 --> 00:09:13,093
Okay.

138
00:09:13,093 --> 00:09:14,885
- Her bank account...
- Right.

139
00:09:21,061 --> 00:09:23,438
Come out already! Hurry up!

140
00:09:23,438 --> 00:09:26,203
Time is money for me, even if it's not for you.

141
00:09:26,203 --> 00:09:28,322
Come out already!

142
00:09:29,233 --> 00:09:31,300
What's wrong with her?

143
00:09:35,617 --> 00:09:36,994
Give it to me. Give it.

144
00:09:36,994 --> 00:09:38,709
Give it.

145
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:41,872
Let's go.

146
00:09:43,125 --> 00:09:45,111
- This is really heavy.
- Yes, it is.

147
00:09:47,004 --> 00:09:48,721
Hey, hey. Big news.

148
00:09:48,721 --> 00:09:50,813
What? What is it?

149
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:54,595
Kim Jin Mi's suspension is confirmed.

150
00:09:54,595 --> 00:09:58,265
Crazy. A suspension?
I haven't heard that word in ages.

151
00:09:58,265 --> 00:10:03,775
Well, she really went too far.
Kim Jin Mi gave me the creeps.

152
00:10:04,646 --> 00:10:08,435
But why isn't Sung Sae Ryeong here again?

153
00:10:08,435 --> 00:10:10,151
You still don't know?

154
00:10:10,151 --> 00:10:12,937
- Hey. They say she slit it.
- Slit what?

155
00:10:12,937 --> 00:10:15,124
Her wrist. At the pool.

156
00:10:15,124 --> 00:10:16,407
- Her wrist?
- Yes.

157
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:17,687
- You don't know?
- Her wrist?

158
00:10:17,687 --> 00:10:19,381
- At the pool.
- Really?

159
00:10:26,627 --> 00:10:28,056
Hurry, hurry!

160
00:10:28,056 --> 00:10:29,402
The teacher...

161
00:10:30,351 --> 00:10:32,606
Please, just sit down. Sit.

162
00:10:33,344 --> 00:10:35,844
- Class President.
- Here.

163
00:10:35,844 --> 00:10:38,888
It looks like it's just a cold.

164
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:40,781
I'll go buy some medicine.

165
00:10:40,781 --> 00:10:43,870
I have to go to the factory anyway
because of a machine issue.

166
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:45,429
I'll buy it on my way back.

167
00:10:45,429 --> 00:10:46,576
Don't worry too much.

168
00:10:46,576 --> 00:10:49,107
What about the hospital? Shouldn't he go?

169
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:50,971
Let's have him take medicine first.

170
00:10:50,971 --> 00:10:53,805
If the fever doesn't drop, we'll go.

171
00:10:54,432 --> 00:10:55,984
Don't worry too much.

172
00:10:56,615 --> 00:10:59,256
How can I not worry? His fever is 39 degrees.

173
00:11:00,292 --> 00:11:01,767
I'll be back.

174
00:11:35,963 --> 00:11:40,111
My baby. Don't ever do this again.

175
00:11:40,882 --> 00:11:45,413
Grandma will die without you.

176
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:47,052
I know, Grandma.

177
00:11:47,052 --> 00:11:49,709
I won't do it again.

178
00:11:49,709 --> 00:11:52,086
You really mustn't. Promise?

179
00:11:52,086 --> 00:11:53,880
Yes. Don't worry.

180
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:56,967
I really have no reason to die now.

181
00:11:56,967 --> 00:11:58,177
Really?

182
00:11:58,177 --> 00:11:59,673
Yes.

183
00:12:00,679 --> 00:12:03,399
Because Yu Gyeom...

184
00:12:07,686 --> 00:12:10,370
He can't abandon me anymore.

185
00:12:18,030 --> 00:12:19,389
I...

186
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:24,567
I like it when you're in the water,
going the farthest.

187
00:12:47,768 --> 00:12:49,170
Yu Gyeom.

188
00:13:47,578 --> 00:13:50,086
If I meet you again,

189
00:13:51,854 --> 00:13:54,499
it'll be the moment I watch you do it.

190
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:09,390
[The 22nd National Swimming Championships]

191
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:13,144
Sir, since we're in Seoul,
should we go to an amusement park?

192
00:14:13,144 --> 00:14:15,188
I'm so pumped right now.

193
00:14:15,188 --> 00:14:19,497
Jeong Uk, how about using that time
to shave off 0.01 seconds?

194
00:14:19,497 --> 00:14:22,920
Shave off 0.01 and the gap with Yu Gyeom
will be 2.99 seconds, not 3.

195
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:25,198
Sir, I told you I shaved off more than that.

196
00:14:25,198 --> 00:14:26,783
I shaved off 0.12 seconds.

197
00:14:26,783 --> 00:14:28,304
Alright, good job.

198
00:14:28,304 --> 00:14:29,560
Let's go eat.

199
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:30,746
Go eat.

200
00:14:30,746 --> 00:14:32,955
Good grief!

201
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:36,209
They keep calling. I said I'm not doing it.

202
00:14:36,209 --> 00:14:38,972
Yes, I'm not buying. I won't sign up.

203
00:14:38,972 --> 00:14:41,073
Sir, it's Yu Gyeom.

204
00:14:41,073 --> 00:14:42,856
What's going on with you?

205
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:47,842
I want to enter the competition, sir.

206
00:14:47,842 --> 00:14:49,639
What?

207
00:14:49,639 --> 00:14:50,807
Hey!

208
00:14:50,807 --> 00:14:53,364
I want to enter the competition, sir.

209
00:14:57,648 --> 00:14:59,444
Sir. I...

210
00:15:00,691 --> 00:15:03,693
I won't stop after just one try
like my father did.

211
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:06,827
I'll do it once.

212
00:15:06,827 --> 00:15:08,417
I'll do it twice.

213
00:15:10,118 --> 00:15:12,203
I'm going to go all the way.

214
00:15:12,203 --> 00:15:16,487
Hey, hurry up and give me your ID number.

215
00:15:18,836 --> 00:15:21,194
I'll head over there now, sir.

216
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:25,925
What? Registration will be closed by then.
I'm in Seoul.

217
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:29,387
- Where are you going?
- You have email, right? Send it.

218
00:15:29,387 --> 00:15:30,847
No. What do you mean, school?

219
00:15:30,847 --> 00:15:32,891
Dad said you need a full day's rest.

220
00:15:32,891 --> 00:15:34,684
Your fever might come back.

221
00:15:34,684 --> 00:15:36,003
And you have to eat later.

222
00:15:36,003 --> 00:15:37,062
I'll be back.

223
00:15:37,062 --> 00:15:40,583
Hey! Yu Gyeom! Cho Yu Gyeom!

224
00:15:50,659 --> 00:15:51,975
I...

225
00:15:53,337 --> 00:15:55,908
I want to see you in the sea.

226
00:16:14,818 --> 00:16:16,586
Why didn't you come yesterday?

227
00:16:18,478 --> 00:16:20,114
What are you doing?

228
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:27,528
Hey, lend me your phone.

229
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:29,596
- Why?
- Hurry.

230
00:16:29,596 --> 00:16:30,855
What are you doing?

231
00:16:36,747 --> 00:16:38,456
What are you doing?

232
00:16:38,456 --> 00:16:40,792
I don't want to carry your photo.

233
00:16:40,792 --> 00:16:44,770
I'm not giving my precious face to you either.

234
00:16:45,964 --> 00:16:47,258
Seriously.

235
00:16:50,806 --> 00:16:52,408
I just registered you.

236
00:16:52,408 --> 00:16:54,054
Really?

237
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:55,183
Thank you, sir.

238
00:16:55,183 --> 00:16:57,475
Hey, by the way...

239
00:16:58,060 --> 00:17:01,354
You know you're applying independently, right?

240
00:17:01,354 --> 00:17:05,733
We planned to sponsor just one student,
but I just squeezed you in.

241
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:09,153
I can't exactly pull Jeong Uk out now.

242
00:17:09,153 --> 00:17:14,951
That swimming nut couldn't sleep last night
fearing you would suddenly enter.

243
00:17:14,951 --> 00:17:17,332
But the prelims are in three days. You know?

244
00:17:17,332 --> 00:17:18,612
Yes, I know.

245
00:17:18,612 --> 00:17:22,417
Without school support,
you'll get a lousy lane. You know that too?

246
00:17:22,417 --> 00:17:24,267
Yes, I know.

247
00:17:25,272 --> 00:17:26,984
You're confident, aren't you?

248
00:17:29,006 --> 00:17:32,415
No, I'm not.

249
00:17:32,415 --> 00:17:33,803
What?

250
00:17:33,803 --> 00:17:35,131
But...

251
00:17:37,429 --> 00:17:39,135
I'll do my best.

252
00:17:40,686 --> 00:17:43,166
Okay. I'll see you down there.

253
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:49,116
Compete in good faith.

254
00:17:49,116 --> 00:17:50,152
Yes, sir.

255
00:17:50,152 --> 00:17:53,072
- Good luck.
- Good luck.

256
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:55,221
Spoken like true men.

257
00:17:55,221 --> 00:17:56,569
Jeong Uk.

258
00:17:56,569 --> 00:17:58,649
- You're the coach?
- Yes, I am.

259
00:17:58,649 --> 00:18:00,204
- Really?
- He's the athlete I trained.

260
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:01,744
- See you later.
- Okay.

261
00:18:01,744 --> 00:18:03,958
- See you later.
- Goodbye.

262
00:18:03,958 --> 00:18:08,280
Hey, so Cho Yu Gyeom is
entering the competition.

263
00:18:10,549 --> 00:18:12,508
No, sir.

264
00:18:12,508 --> 00:18:14,845
What do you mean, no? You're entering too.

265
00:18:14,845 --> 00:18:18,015
If Yu Gyeom enters, I'll lose.

266
00:18:18,015 --> 00:18:19,224
Look at this guy.

267
00:18:19,224 --> 00:18:22,439
How do you know? With your confidence...

268
00:18:23,359 --> 00:18:24,655
No.

269
00:18:25,687 --> 00:18:28,443
My confidence just plummeted.

270
00:18:28,443 --> 00:18:30,119
It's a total crash.

271
00:18:31,153 --> 00:18:33,253
Should I buy you beef?

272
00:18:34,239 --> 00:18:35,602
Wait, no.

273
00:18:36,575 --> 00:18:38,353
My confidence just skyrocketed.

274
00:18:38,979 --> 00:18:40,485
You little...

275
00:18:41,890 --> 00:18:43,115
What's with you?

276
00:18:44,133 --> 00:18:45,397
What?

277
00:18:45,397 --> 00:18:47,094
What are you signing up for?

278
00:18:49,846 --> 00:18:50,923
The swimming competition.

279
00:18:50,923 --> 00:18:52,136
What?

280
00:18:53,323 --> 00:18:55,181
Is that something to shout about?

281
00:18:55,181 --> 00:18:57,054
Of course it is.

282
00:18:57,054 --> 00:18:58,173
Why?

283
00:18:58,764 --> 00:18:59,815
Why?

284
00:19:00,638 --> 00:19:02,475
I should be asking you that.

285
00:19:02,475 --> 00:19:04,103
Why on earth are you doing this?

286
00:19:05,936 --> 00:19:09,278
Because I want to.

287
00:19:09,278 --> 00:19:10,441
No.

288
00:19:10,441 --> 00:19:13,303
You have always wanted to, but you never did.

289
00:19:13,303 --> 00:19:16,051
What suddenly changed your mind?

290
00:19:18,217 --> 00:19:19,689
Cho Yu Gyeom.

291
00:19:27,937 --> 00:19:29,572
I'm out of the hospital.

292
00:19:30,755 --> 00:19:32,887
Won't you ask if I'm okay?

293
00:19:33,758 --> 00:19:34,799
Are you okay?

294
00:19:34,799 --> 00:19:35,935
Yes.

295
00:19:35,935 --> 00:19:39,491
I'm fine because you were there.

296
00:19:41,389 --> 00:19:42,860
What?

297
00:19:42,860 --> 00:19:44,396
Are you going to hit me?

298
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:49,911
But Yu Gyeom...

299
00:19:50,844 --> 00:19:52,978
Listen.

300
00:19:52,978 --> 00:19:55,834
Don't ever let go of this again.

301
00:19:55,834 --> 00:19:57,045
Okay?

302
00:19:58,444 --> 00:19:59,783
Never again.

303
00:20:05,398 --> 00:20:06,426
I won't.

304
00:20:06,426 --> 00:20:07,841
I promise.

305
00:20:30,061 --> 00:20:34,100
- Right. You really should never get married.
- Really.

306
00:20:35,586 --> 00:20:39,526
When I was young, my aunt, a college
student, came to visit our house.

307
00:20:40,322 --> 00:20:43,011
Ha Yeon, are you done playing?

308
00:20:43,011 --> 00:20:45,385
Come here, come here.

309
00:20:46,245 --> 00:20:47,664
Do you only like your aunt?

310
00:20:47,664 --> 00:20:50,270
The clothes my aunt wore looked pretty.

311
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:08,107
So when she wasn't around,
I secretly wore them in front of the mirror...

312
00:21:09,228 --> 00:21:11,039
Wait for me.

313
00:21:28,664 --> 00:21:32,634
But they didn't suit me at all.

314
00:21:42,551 --> 00:21:44,608
My aunt looked so pretty in them.

315
00:21:45,541 --> 00:21:48,642
Nevertheless, I had one wish.

316
00:21:48,642 --> 00:21:49,669
What?

317
00:21:49,669 --> 00:21:52,429
I wanted them to suit me well.

318
00:21:52,429 --> 00:21:53,939
- Why are you crying?
- Kim Ha Yeon.

319
00:21:53,939 --> 00:21:56,455
- For them to fit me perfectly.
- Isn't this your aunt's outfit?

320
00:22:04,449 --> 00:22:06,816
I wanted them to like me.

321
00:22:07,786 --> 00:22:09,894
I wanted them to like me
as much as I liked them.

322
00:22:13,625 --> 00:22:16,962
An eighteen-year-old's sadness
isn't necessarily mature.

323
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:21,341
I still cry.

324
00:22:21,341 --> 00:22:26,006
For the same reason I did when I was seven.

325
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:36,290
I didn't know there was a place like this here.

326
00:22:36,290 --> 00:22:38,350
This is all there is around here.

327
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:41,100
- This spot looks good.
- Yes.

328
00:22:47,836 --> 00:22:51,421
But aren't you tired, Jung Yeon?

329
00:22:51,421 --> 00:22:52,971
What?

330
00:22:52,971 --> 00:22:54,625
- Me?
- Yes.

331
00:22:54,625 --> 00:22:57,458
You look like you haven't slept at all.

332
00:22:58,545 --> 00:23:01,796
No, I did sleep.

333
00:23:05,149 --> 00:23:08,989
Actually, I have something
I'm really curious about.

334
00:23:10,010 --> 00:23:11,500
Then go ahead and ask.

335
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:15,455
Why did you decide to date me?

336
00:23:15,455 --> 00:23:17,220
Do you like me?

337
00:23:18,906 --> 00:23:20,304
No.

338
00:23:20,304 --> 00:23:21,730
Not yet.

339
00:23:24,321 --> 00:23:25,989
I knew it.

340
00:23:26,771 --> 00:23:29,159
Then why did you decide to date me?

341
00:23:29,159 --> 00:23:32,367
Is it to learn sign language
to your heart's content?

342
00:23:34,038 --> 00:23:35,867
Am I that kind of person?

343
00:23:35,867 --> 00:23:38,357
No, I'm that kind of person.

344
00:23:40,979 --> 00:23:46,401
I have just stopped rejecting people
who confess to me.

345
00:23:51,764 --> 00:23:53,640
Not the answer you expected, right?

346
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,851
I'm really glad I confessed then.

347
00:23:55,851 --> 00:23:57,019
Pardon?

348
00:23:57,019 --> 00:24:00,314
Then what about that Hye Min person?

349
00:24:00,314 --> 00:24:02,418
Didn't you reject her too?

350
00:24:02,418 --> 00:24:04,667
I did reject her.

351
00:24:04,667 --> 00:24:06,976
Then that's a bit inconsistent, isn't it?

352
00:24:06,976 --> 00:24:09,171
It only started from a certain point.

353
00:24:13,036 --> 00:24:16,510
You certainly have a lot of questions.

354
00:24:16,510 --> 00:24:19,195
Yes, I hear that a lot.

355
00:24:19,195 --> 00:24:22,173
My mom even tells me I'm too noisy.

356
00:24:22,173 --> 00:24:24,402
But my grandpa likes it when I chatter.

357
00:24:24,402 --> 00:24:26,850
He said I'm like a chirping lark.

358
00:24:30,448 --> 00:24:36,720
But why did you stop rejecting
people who confess to you?

359
00:24:37,319 --> 00:24:38,684
I just...

360
00:24:39,269 --> 00:24:41,738
I can't do that anymore.

361
00:24:41,738 --> 00:24:46,192
I'm asking why you can't do that anymore.

362
00:24:48,362 --> 00:24:49,768
Is that a lunch box?

363
00:24:49,768 --> 00:24:51,346
Yes.

364
00:24:51,346 --> 00:24:53,145
I made it myself.

365
00:24:53,145 --> 00:24:55,155
It looks delicious.

366
00:24:55,155 --> 00:24:56,499
Wait a second.

367
00:25:04,688 --> 00:25:07,346
But I really hope for one thing.

368
00:25:07,346 --> 00:25:09,383
It shouldn't be out of guilt.

369
00:25:09,383 --> 00:25:11,139
You know, that kind of thing.

370
00:25:11,139 --> 00:25:15,492
Accepting me because you're afraid
I'll suffer if you reject me?

371
00:25:19,375 --> 00:25:20,695
That's...

372
00:25:22,231 --> 00:25:24,274
I don't think it's guilt.

373
00:25:24,274 --> 00:25:26,026
Really?

374
00:25:26,026 --> 00:25:28,614
Then is it a sense of responsibility?

375
00:25:29,778 --> 00:25:30,792
It's delicious.

376
00:25:30,792 --> 00:25:32,351
Really?

377
00:25:32,351 --> 00:25:33,881
I'm so glad.

378
00:25:37,810 --> 00:25:41,694
You know, Jung Yeon, I want you to like me.

379
00:25:43,666 --> 00:25:45,975
Please like me, Jung Yeon.

380
00:25:47,455 --> 00:25:49,155
Please like me.

381
00:25:53,136 --> 00:25:54,891
I'll work hard for it.

382
00:26:00,184 --> 00:26:06,167
I know it's not something I can just ask for,
but I'll work hard for it.

383
00:26:11,679 --> 00:26:12,876
Why?

384
00:26:16,660 --> 00:26:17,908
No.

385
00:26:18,589 --> 00:26:19,894
It's nothing.

386
00:26:23,081 --> 00:26:25,262
- Hey, what should we eat?
- Burgers.

387
00:26:25,262 --> 00:26:26,819
- No. I don't like it.
- How about hamburgers?

388
00:26:26,819 --> 00:26:28,714
- Good.
- Why won't you eat burgers?

389
00:26:28,714 --> 00:26:30,340
- No reason.
- Are you getting a burger?

390
00:26:30,340 --> 00:26:31,841
I'm not getting a burger.

391
00:26:34,261 --> 00:26:35,429
Pizza. How about pizza?

392
00:26:35,429 --> 00:26:37,592
- No.
- Pizza?

393
00:26:39,057 --> 00:26:40,381
Why? Aren't you going?

394
00:26:41,457 --> 00:26:42,839
Go ahead.

395
00:26:42,839 --> 00:26:44,061
Why?

396
00:26:44,061 --> 00:26:45,628
I'm going to practice first.

397
00:26:45,628 --> 00:26:46,826
Practice?

398
00:26:46,826 --> 00:26:48,140
For what?

399
00:26:48,140 --> 00:26:49,346
He's entering the swim meet.

400
00:26:49,346 --> 00:26:51,611
- What?
- Why?

401
00:26:51,611 --> 00:26:53,195
Go on. I'll go after practice.

402
00:26:53,195 --> 00:26:54,720
What's this about?

403
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:57,971
You're really entering the meet?

404
00:26:57,971 --> 00:26:59,034
Hey!

405
00:26:59,034 --> 00:27:01,141
Yes, he is.

406
00:27:01,141 --> 00:27:02,346
Holy moly.

407
00:27:02,346 --> 00:27:04,377
Guacamole. Let's go.

408
00:27:17,159 --> 00:27:18,208
Hey.

409
00:27:19,431 --> 00:27:20,517
Well...

410
00:27:21,391 --> 00:27:23,696
Sorry for joining the meet so suddenly.

411
00:27:24,353 --> 00:27:25,823
It's okay.

412
00:27:25,823 --> 00:27:27,856
It's actually a relief.

413
00:27:27,856 --> 00:27:29,091
Why?

414
00:27:30,053 --> 00:27:34,945
I had a dream that you suddenly
entered the competition.

415
00:27:34,945 --> 00:27:36,907
I heard about that.

416
00:27:36,907 --> 00:27:40,617
But come to think of it,
that dream came true, right?

417
00:27:40,617 --> 00:27:42,952
Yes. But why is it a relief?

418
00:27:44,166 --> 00:27:45,913
Because in my dream...

419
00:27:47,626 --> 00:27:48,885
In the end...

420
00:27:53,307 --> 00:27:54,872
I beat you.

421
00:27:57,045 --> 00:27:59,844
Let's do our best, Cho Yu Gyeom.

422
00:28:04,885 --> 00:28:06,422
Kim Ha Yeon, you.

423
00:28:09,992 --> 00:28:11,294
What?

424
00:28:13,487 --> 00:28:17,383
Can't you please talk to me?

425
00:28:20,412 --> 00:28:22,164
Talk now.

426
00:28:22,164 --> 00:28:24,368
You're not this kind of person.

427
00:28:24,368 --> 00:28:26,663
Someone so out of control.

428
00:28:26,663 --> 00:28:29,501
Someone who's such a mess.

429
00:28:29,501 --> 00:28:31,596
That's not you.

430
00:28:31,596 --> 00:28:32,839
Is it?

431
00:28:36,936 --> 00:28:38,869
Then tell me.

432
00:28:40,796 --> 00:28:42,950
Were you perfect, Mom?

433
00:28:44,005 --> 00:28:45,120
What?

434
00:28:45,120 --> 00:28:46,721
I mean you, Mom.

435
00:28:47,613 --> 00:28:50,387
Were you perfect when you were my age?

436
00:28:50,387 --> 00:28:52,090
Were you okay?

437
00:28:54,608 --> 00:28:58,450
I was fine.

438
00:28:58,450 --> 00:29:01,582
I listened to your grandmother.

439
00:29:01,582 --> 00:29:03,021
And on the inside?

440
00:29:03,742 --> 00:29:05,464
What?

441
00:29:05,464 --> 00:29:06,495
On the inside?

442
00:29:06,495 --> 00:29:08,721
Was your heart okay?

443
00:29:08,721 --> 00:29:10,773
Without any waves?

444
00:29:11,708 --> 00:29:15,369
Are you talking about teenage angst right now?

445
00:29:15,962 --> 00:29:17,218
No.

446
00:29:18,500 --> 00:29:21,325
I'm just talking about being my age.

447
00:29:21,325 --> 00:29:25,804
The age when earthquakes, typhoons, fires,
and whirlwinds rage in your heart.

448
00:29:27,212 --> 00:29:32,767
I don't think you were perfect
at my age just because you're my mom.

449
00:29:33,470 --> 00:29:35,703
How can anyone live like that?

450
00:29:36,429 --> 00:29:42,407
Some days are fine, some days are a mess,
and then some days are fine again.

451
00:29:42,407 --> 00:29:44,177
That's how life is.

452
00:29:51,124 --> 00:29:54,122
Mom, give me something to eat.

453
00:29:56,547 --> 00:29:58,537
Can you say that again?

454
00:29:59,140 --> 00:30:02,672
I don't understand.

455
00:30:06,258 --> 00:30:10,674
I'm saying I'm like this because
being my age is a mess.

456
00:30:11,772 --> 00:30:14,595
Not because I'm a mess.

457
00:30:17,029 --> 00:30:18,412
Mom.

458
00:30:21,349 --> 00:30:23,412
You know...

459
00:30:23,999 --> 00:30:28,430
I'm sure you were just like me
when you were my age.

460
00:30:28,430 --> 00:30:30,591
I'm leaving now.

461
00:30:45,332 --> 00:30:46,614
Mom.

462
00:30:47,598 --> 00:30:49,291
Some food...

463
00:30:50,357 --> 00:30:52,419
Can you get it yourself?

464
00:30:54,886 --> 00:30:56,179
Right.

465
00:30:56,179 --> 00:30:58,383
We'll leave in the afternoon.

466
00:30:59,149 --> 00:31:01,109
Did you all pack your bags?

467
00:31:01,109 --> 00:31:02,368
Yes, sir.

468
00:31:02,368 --> 00:31:03,957
Jeong Uk is in lane 3.

469
00:31:03,957 --> 00:31:05,484
Yu Gyeom is...

470
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:07,990
You are in lane 8.

471
00:31:07,990 --> 00:31:10,850
Cho Yu Gyeom, you brought this on yourself.

472
00:31:10,850 --> 00:31:11,973
Yes, sir.

473
00:31:11,973 --> 00:31:12,996
Good.

474
00:31:12,996 --> 00:31:14,721
Then come here after lunch.

475
00:31:14,721 --> 00:31:15,876
Let's head out together.

476
00:31:15,876 --> 00:31:17,012
Yes, sir.

477
00:31:17,012 --> 00:31:18,695
Hey, see you later.

478
00:31:21,734 --> 00:31:23,642
Right. Cho Yu Gyeom.

479
00:31:25,524 --> 00:31:27,587
You're not...

480
00:31:28,179 --> 00:31:29,464
You know...

481
00:31:30,474 --> 00:31:33,485
You're not going to the competition
without telling your family, are you?

482
00:31:34,458 --> 00:31:35,477
I haven't told them.

483
00:31:35,477 --> 00:31:37,979
What? Why?

484
00:31:37,979 --> 00:31:39,669
I just wasn't going to tell them.

485
00:31:39,669 --> 00:31:43,700
What? No. If you don't tell them, I'll have to.

486
00:31:44,333 --> 00:31:45,763
Call them now.

487
00:31:45,763 --> 00:31:46,930
Hurry.

488
00:31:46,930 --> 00:31:48,091
Go on.

489
00:31:48,909 --> 00:31:51,211
Just tell them, man. Do it.

490
00:32:12,599 --> 00:32:15,127
I need to check that.

491
00:32:15,127 --> 00:32:16,717
Sam Hee.

492
00:32:17,439 --> 00:32:19,006
Where did she go?

493
00:32:20,318 --> 00:32:21,508
Yes. Hello?

494
00:32:21,508 --> 00:32:22,566
Mom.

495
00:32:22,566 --> 00:32:23,984
Yu Gyeom.

496
00:32:23,984 --> 00:32:26,719
Is something wrong? I'm busy right now.

497
00:32:26,719 --> 00:32:28,704
I'm going to a swim meet.

498
00:32:29,322 --> 00:32:30,498
What?

499
00:32:30,498 --> 00:32:32,373
I'm going to a swim meet.

500
00:32:34,870 --> 00:32:36,974
Are you just notifying me?

501
00:32:36,974 --> 00:32:38,358
Yes, I am.

502
00:32:38,358 --> 00:32:39,595
I'm sorry.

503
00:32:42,671 --> 00:32:43,991
Hello?

504
00:32:45,523 --> 00:32:46,702
Mom?

505
00:32:48,341 --> 00:32:50,051
When is it?

506
00:32:50,051 --> 00:32:51,597
Tomorrow.

507
00:32:51,597 --> 00:32:53,513
Tomorrow?

508
00:32:53,513 --> 00:32:57,976
Right. If it's tomorrow,
first we have the ancestral rite today.

509
00:32:57,976 --> 00:33:01,009
I'll sleep in Seoul today
and come back after the meet.

510
00:33:01,009 --> 00:33:02,232
No, Cho Yu Gyeom.

511
00:33:02,232 --> 00:33:03,869
Absolutely not.

512
00:33:03,869 --> 00:33:06,113
You have an ancestral rite today.

513
00:33:07,694 --> 00:33:10,354
What are you going to tell your grandfather?

514
00:33:10,354 --> 00:33:11,835
It doesn't matter what you say.

515
00:33:11,835 --> 00:33:16,244
You can't go to the meet,
and you definitely can't miss the rite.

516
00:33:16,244 --> 00:33:18,942
What kind of heir would miss an ancestral rite?

517
00:33:18,942 --> 00:33:22,218
Ma'am, you shouldn't take that over there.

518
00:33:22,959 --> 00:33:25,740
Yu Gyeom, Mom will...

519
00:33:25,740 --> 00:33:27,796
I don't want to live like Dad.

520
00:33:31,635 --> 00:33:33,847
Please contact me anytime.

521
00:33:33,847 --> 00:33:35,473
I'm honored.

522
00:33:41,788 --> 00:33:44,233
- Hello.
- Hello.

523
00:33:44,233 --> 00:33:46,302
I don't want to live like Dad.

524
00:33:47,005 --> 00:33:49,530
But at this rate, Mom...

525
00:33:49,530 --> 00:33:51,753
I'll definitely end up like him.

526
00:33:52,816 --> 00:33:54,687
Mom, seriously...

527
00:33:58,896 --> 00:34:00,512
Isn't that just too terrible?

528
00:34:05,943 --> 00:34:09,381
Ma'am, where should I put the japchae?

529
00:34:09,381 --> 00:34:11,758
Ma'am, is this enough fish?

530
00:34:11,758 --> 00:34:13,802
Ma'am, the elder is looking for you.

531
00:34:13,802 --> 00:34:16,278
Ma'am, should I brown the bulgogi more?

532
00:34:16,278 --> 00:34:19,140
Ma'am, should I fry more meat patties?

533
00:34:19,140 --> 00:34:20,568
Ma'am.

534
00:34:33,008 --> 00:34:34,279
Yes.

535
00:34:35,566 --> 00:34:37,043
It is terrible.

536
00:34:42,159 --> 00:34:43,405
Go.

537
00:34:45,046 --> 00:34:46,876
Thanks, Mom. About Grandpa...

538
00:34:46,876 --> 00:34:48,922
I'll take care of that.

539
00:34:48,922 --> 00:34:50,469
Okay.

540
00:34:52,096 --> 00:34:53,645
Alright.

541
00:34:53,645 --> 00:34:55,979
Good luck, son.

542
00:34:55,979 --> 00:34:57,196
Yes.

543
00:34:57,196 --> 00:34:58,462
Son.

544
00:35:02,561 --> 00:35:05,004
Say hello. I'm your father.

545
00:35:06,813 --> 00:35:10,113
- Hello. Father.
- Right. My son.

546
00:35:10,113 --> 00:35:13,566
It's good to see you at school.

547
00:35:14,248 --> 00:35:16,163
I can't make the ancestral rite today.

548
00:35:16,163 --> 00:35:17,406
What?

549
00:35:18,171 --> 00:35:21,521
Father, please explain it well
to Grandpa for me.

550
00:35:24,666 --> 00:35:26,638
Why can't you come to the rite?

551
00:35:26,638 --> 00:35:28,178
No.

552
00:35:29,087 --> 00:35:31,796
Isn't it better for you to tell him
rather than Mom?

553
00:35:31,796 --> 00:35:33,466
You can take a hit better.

554
00:35:33,466 --> 00:35:35,282
What are you talking about?

555
00:35:35,282 --> 00:35:38,587
No. You have to attend the rite.
You absolutely must!

556
00:35:39,848 --> 00:35:41,997
I'm entering a swim meet.

557
00:35:45,562 --> 00:35:47,302
I'm leaving now, Father.

558
00:35:55,030 --> 00:35:56,228
Honestly!

559
00:35:59,908 --> 00:36:01,659
No, wait...

560
00:36:01,659 --> 00:36:04,915
Yu Gyeom is very clear about his opinions.

561
00:36:04,915 --> 00:36:06,554
I'll go give him a talking-to.

562
00:36:06,554 --> 00:36:08,921
Yu Gyeom! Cho Yu Gyeom!

563
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:17,384
Hey, hey!

564
00:36:17,384 --> 00:36:19,969
Is Cho Yu Gyeom really entering? No way, right?

565
00:36:19,969 --> 00:36:22,138
No, it's true.

566
00:36:22,138 --> 00:36:24,459
I heard he's going to Seoul today.

567
00:36:24,459 --> 00:36:27,551
Holy moly guacamole roly-poly.

568
00:36:28,853 --> 00:36:31,476
That's such an outdated expression.

569
00:36:31,476 --> 00:36:33,691
Sae Ryeong, did you talk him into it?

570
00:36:33,691 --> 00:36:35,985
Into entering the competition?

571
00:36:35,985 --> 00:36:37,017
What?

572
00:36:37,017 --> 00:36:41,259
I mean, Cho Yu Gyeom never entered
competitions no matter how good he was.

573
00:36:41,259 --> 00:36:42,713
But now he is.

574
00:36:42,713 --> 00:36:45,296
That means you convinced him, right?

575
00:36:49,499 --> 00:36:53,755
Sae Ryeong, then you're going
to Seoul tomorrow too. Right?

576
00:36:53,755 --> 00:36:55,293
Why would I go to Seoul?

577
00:36:55,293 --> 00:36:56,346
Why else?

578
00:36:56,346 --> 00:36:58,031
To cheer for Yu Gyeom.

579
00:37:00,969 --> 00:37:02,137
What?

580
00:37:02,137 --> 00:37:03,640
You weren't planning to go?

581
00:37:03,640 --> 00:37:07,313
He's doing this because of you.
How can you not go?

582
00:37:10,692 --> 00:37:11,804
Right.

583
00:37:11,804 --> 00:37:13,137
I'm his girlfriend.

584
00:37:13,137 --> 00:37:14,863
I definitely have to go.

585
00:37:14,863 --> 00:37:18,141
Yu Gyeom is entering the competition
for me, right?

586
00:37:18,141 --> 00:37:19,863
- Want to come too?
- Really?

587
00:37:19,863 --> 00:37:21,418
I'm in! I would love to.

588
00:37:21,418 --> 00:37:22,824
Awesome.

589
00:37:22,824 --> 00:37:24,284
I'll ask Yu Gyeom.

590
00:37:24,284 --> 00:37:27,347
Hey, Sung Sae Ryeong.
Ask for us too, so we can all go.

591
00:37:27,347 --> 00:37:28,900
Lee Won Bae. You're going, right?

592
00:37:28,900 --> 00:37:31,213
Why would I...

593
00:37:31,213 --> 00:37:34,138
Let's go see Seoul for a change.

594
00:37:34,138 --> 00:37:35,214
It'll be a nice change.

595
00:37:35,214 --> 00:37:38,637
What change of pace?

596
00:37:38,637 --> 00:37:40,043
Lee Won Bae.

597
00:37:41,211 --> 00:37:42,673
What?

598
00:37:46,249 --> 00:37:47,809
Come out here for a second.

599
00:37:48,938 --> 00:37:50,101
Yu Gyeom, you're here?

600
00:37:50,101 --> 00:37:51,990
Yes, Lord Yu Gyeom.

601
00:37:51,990 --> 00:37:54,058
I'm coming.

602
00:37:58,487 --> 00:38:00,396
Then for me, the sea...

603
00:38:02,814 --> 00:38:07,100
I want to swim with all my strength
as far as I can go.

604
00:38:08,291 --> 00:38:09,917
That's my dream.

605
00:39:59,154 --> 00:40:01,462
This is your first warning.

606
00:40:04,182 --> 00:40:05,557
Why?

607
00:40:06,772 --> 00:40:11,160
Next time, I won't care if you're hurt
or not. Get out.

608
00:40:13,747 --> 00:40:16,664
Do you happen to have a girlfriend?

609
00:40:16,664 --> 00:40:19,125
Slow down a bit.

610
00:40:19,125 --> 00:40:23,717
I asked if you have a girlfriend.

611
00:40:25,509 --> 00:40:26,997
I do.

612
00:40:30,517 --> 00:40:31,804
Hey.

613
00:40:31,804 --> 00:40:35,284
Because I'm 30 now.

614
00:40:35,284 --> 00:40:36,911
So I see her sometimes.

615
00:40:39,231 --> 00:40:41,522
The girl you're dating?

616
00:40:41,522 --> 00:40:43,015
Who would date me?

617
00:40:43,015 --> 00:40:45,514
I leave dates whenever I get a call.

618
00:40:45,514 --> 00:40:50,553
We just meet up sometimes.

619
00:40:53,242 --> 00:40:54,997
Then that's fine.

620
00:40:54,997 --> 00:40:56,297
Fine?

621
00:40:59,926 --> 00:41:02,131
Fine? What's fine?

622
00:41:05,757 --> 00:41:07,727
What do you mean by that?

623
00:41:07,727 --> 00:41:08,995
Hey!

624
00:41:10,486 --> 00:41:12,519
She can't hear me.

625
00:41:20,561 --> 00:41:21,732
[A Family of Scholars]

626
00:41:23,942 --> 00:41:25,198
Honey.

627
00:41:29,891 --> 00:41:31,994
You'll talk about Yu Gyeom, right?

628
00:41:34,227 --> 00:41:36,997
Father. It's Jae Jin.

629
00:41:36,997 --> 00:41:38,912
Come in.

630
00:41:41,335 --> 00:41:43,413
I'll do it. Let me.

631
00:41:44,166 --> 00:41:45,863
I'm good at taking hits.

632
00:41:53,572 --> 00:41:55,242
What?

633
00:41:56,804 --> 00:41:58,006
Well...

634
00:41:58,818 --> 00:42:00,423
You see...

635
00:42:00,423 --> 00:42:01,921
Yu Gyeom...

636
00:42:02,687 --> 00:42:05,992
He won't be able to attend the ancestral rite.

637
00:42:05,992 --> 00:42:07,684
Yu Gyeom's father.

638
00:42:07,684 --> 00:42:10,164
Does that make any sense?

639
00:42:10,164 --> 00:42:12,704
I know it doesn't.

640
00:42:13,558 --> 00:42:14,871
But Father.

641
00:42:14,871 --> 00:42:17,744
Yu Gyeom is competing in a major meet--

642
00:42:17,744 --> 00:42:20,361
Stop talking nonsense and bring him here!

643
00:42:39,476 --> 00:42:41,099
Come out here for a second.

644
00:42:43,311 --> 00:42:45,774
Is Cho Yu Gyeom really entering? No way, right?

645
00:42:45,774 --> 00:42:48,313
No, it's true.

646
00:43:00,539 --> 00:43:01,846
Mom.

647
00:43:01,846 --> 00:43:03,498
You have Sung Sae Ryeong's number.

648
00:43:03,498 --> 00:43:05,346
Jeez! You scared me!

649
00:43:05,346 --> 00:43:09,119
You must have her number.
I heard you two even swapped credit cards.

650
00:43:10,213 --> 00:43:11,838
No, well...

651
00:43:12,971 --> 00:43:14,429
I do have it.

652
00:43:14,429 --> 00:43:16,677
Then give it to me.

653
00:43:16,677 --> 00:43:19,454
Hey, don't you have her number?

654
00:43:19,454 --> 00:43:21,766
No, I don't.

655
00:43:21,766 --> 00:43:23,392
Why not?

656
00:43:23,392 --> 00:43:24,471
Mom.

657
00:43:24,471 --> 00:43:28,055
Would you want to swap numbers
with a girl who gave you a concussion?

658
00:43:28,055 --> 00:43:31,496
She also stole your boyfriend.

659
00:43:33,906 --> 00:43:35,866
Hurry.

660
00:43:35,866 --> 00:43:37,411
Fine.

661
00:43:38,950 --> 00:43:41,135
- 010.
- Okay.

662
00:43:41,135 --> 00:43:43,342
0218.

663
00:43:43,342 --> 00:43:44,729
Hey.

664
00:43:44,729 --> 00:43:47,169
You won't cause trouble again, right?

665
00:43:47,169 --> 00:43:49,565
It's not like that. Hurry up.

666
00:43:57,888 --> 00:43:59,205
Hello?

667
00:44:00,162 --> 00:44:01,592
It's Sae Ryeong.

668
00:44:01,592 --> 00:44:02,846
No way.

669
00:44:02,846 --> 00:44:04,186
Sung Sae Ryeong.

670
00:44:04,186 --> 00:44:07,436
Why are you calling me? What's the occasion?

671
00:44:07,436 --> 00:44:09,324
You're with Yu Gyeom, aren't you?

672
00:44:09,324 --> 00:44:10,439
What?

673
00:44:10,439 --> 00:44:12,010
What was that?

674
00:44:12,010 --> 00:44:13,304
Put Yu Gyeom on.

675
00:44:13,304 --> 00:44:15,012
He doesn't have his phone.

676
00:44:16,567 --> 00:44:17,679
I don't want to.

677
00:44:17,679 --> 00:44:18,794
Why?

678
00:44:18,794 --> 00:44:20,324
I just don't.

679
00:44:20,324 --> 00:44:22,473
Call him yourself.

680
00:44:22,473 --> 00:44:24,012
We're at the Fricks Hotel.

681
00:44:24,012 --> 00:44:26,873
He's in room 2001. Happy?

682
00:44:26,873 --> 00:44:29,170
- I'm hanging up.
- Im Jeong Uk.

683
00:44:29,170 --> 00:44:31,707
I know you like me.

684
00:44:33,509 --> 00:44:36,264
I heard your dad owns a golf course.

685
00:44:36,264 --> 00:44:38,386
He has several, right?

686
00:44:42,205 --> 00:44:45,479
Life is long, you know?

687
00:44:46,309 --> 00:44:50,567
[Fricks Hotel]
I'm saying we don't know what the future holds.

688
00:44:50,567 --> 00:44:53,844
But right now, I'm with Cho Yu Gyeom.

689
00:44:53,844 --> 00:44:55,529
Do you understand?

690
00:44:55,529 --> 00:44:57,316
You won't always be...

691
00:44:58,654 --> 00:45:00,907
This crazy girl.

692
00:45:00,907 --> 00:45:04,354
Did you just swear at me?

693
00:45:04,354 --> 00:45:07,173
Why would I swear at you?
Seriously! I'm hanging up.

694
00:45:07,840 --> 00:45:09,293
I'm Kim Ha Yeon.

695
00:45:09,293 --> 00:45:12,588
Sung Sae Ryeong, want to meet?

696
00:45:12,588 --> 00:45:13,993
Right now.

697
00:45:39,293 --> 00:45:41,771
When are you bringing Yu Gyeom home?

698
00:45:48,872 --> 00:45:50,110
Seriously!

699
00:45:55,484 --> 00:45:57,826
[Men's High School 200m Freestyle
Qualifying Round 12]

700
00:46:08,690 --> 00:46:11,893
Why are you guys so nervous?

701
00:46:11,893 --> 00:46:14,355
You don't have to win first place. Don't.

702
00:46:14,355 --> 00:46:16,315
Really, sir? We really don't have to?

703
00:46:16,315 --> 00:46:20,546
Yes, you don't. How can both of you win?
Only one of you needs to take first.

704
00:46:20,546 --> 00:46:24,323
If the vice principal doesn't chew me out,
we're having a beef party.

705
00:46:24,323 --> 00:46:25,658
That's what's important.

706
00:46:25,658 --> 00:46:27,929
Did you just laugh?

707
00:46:27,929 --> 00:46:29,262
Don't be nervous.

708
00:46:29,262 --> 00:46:32,581
But have the mindset
that you'll win even if it kills you.

709
00:46:32,581 --> 00:46:34,336
- Okay? Okay?
- Yes.

710
00:46:34,336 --> 00:46:35,769
Hands in.

711
00:46:36,834 --> 00:46:38,417
One, two, three. Upo!

712
00:46:38,417 --> 00:46:40,234
- Okay!
- Okay.

713
00:46:40,965 --> 00:46:44,427
- We're starting. Athletes, please gather.
- Yes.

714
00:46:44,427 --> 00:46:45,553
Okay.

715
00:46:45,553 --> 00:46:47,081
- Lane 1, Lee Su Chang.
- Yes.

716
00:46:47,081 --> 00:46:48,392
- Lane 2, Ma Gyeong Beom.
- Yes.

717
00:46:48,392 --> 00:46:49,705
- Lane 3, Im Jeong Uk.
- Yes.

718
00:46:49,705 --> 00:46:51,166
- Lane 4, Kim Tae Woon.
- Yes.

719
00:46:51,166 --> 00:46:52,356
- Lane 5, Kim Chan Hyeok.
- Yes.

720
00:46:52,356 --> 00:46:53,769
- Lane 6, Min Seung Gyu.
- Yes.

721
00:46:53,769 --> 00:46:54,869
- Lane 7, Lee Gyu Seong.
- Yes.

722
00:46:54,869 --> 00:46:56,355
- Lane 8, Cho Yu Gyeom.
- Yes.

723
00:46:56,355 --> 00:46:59,493
Okay. Let's enter in order,
starting with lane one.

724
00:47:03,795 --> 00:47:07,999
Next, we'll broadcast the 22nd
National Swimming Championships.

725
00:47:07,999 --> 00:47:14,418
This is the Men's High School 200m Freestyle
Qualifying Round 12.

726
00:47:14,418 --> 00:47:17,111
- The athletes are now entering.
- Yes.

727
00:47:18,461 --> 00:47:21,440
In lane 5, Kim Chan Hyeok, a senior
at Ulsan Sports High School.

728
00:47:21,440 --> 00:47:24,228
In lane 6, Min Seung Gyu, a freshman
at Seoul Sports High School.

729
00:47:24,228 --> 00:47:26,967
Lane 7, Lee Gyu Seong, a sophomore
at Gyeonggi Jeil High School.

730
00:47:26,967 --> 00:47:29,722
Lane 8, Cho Yu Gyeom, a sophomore
at Andong Upo High School.

731
00:47:29,722 --> 00:47:32,558
These eight athletes will compete
in the preliminaries.

732
00:47:32,558 --> 00:47:37,229
The athletes must show off the skills
they have honed for this day.

733
00:47:37,229 --> 00:47:43,078
I'm looking forward to seeing
many new records set today.

734
00:47:54,914 --> 00:47:59,078
Yes, they must have sweated buckets
to prepare for this stage.

735
00:47:59,078 --> 00:48:02,745
They must be feeling very nervous
at this moment before the start.

736
00:48:02,745 --> 00:48:06,008
- That's right. Who gets the best start...
- Yes.

737
00:48:06,008 --> 00:48:10,726
And since it's a 200m race,
they have to do four laps in a 50m pool.

738
00:48:10,726 --> 00:48:15,559
So it's crucial when they decide
to make their final spurt.

739
00:48:15,559 --> 00:48:17,436
The athletes are on the starting blocks.

740
00:48:17,436 --> 00:48:23,153
This is the Men's High School 200m
Freestyle Qualifying Round 12.

741
00:48:30,601 --> 00:48:33,744
Im Jeong Uk is currently taking the lead.

742
00:48:33,744 --> 00:48:36,997
As expected, Im Jeong Uk
of Upo High School stands out.

743
00:48:36,997 --> 00:48:41,168
Right. He showed a very strong spurt
in his previous performance as well.

744
00:48:41,168 --> 00:48:44,004
Good. Go, go!

745
00:48:44,004 --> 00:48:48,759
Isn't Cho Jae Jin, the first Asian to reach
an Olympic final, from this school?

746
00:48:48,759 --> 00:48:52,763
That's right. But there's another athlete
from Upo High School competing.

747
00:48:52,763 --> 00:48:57,493
I heard Cho Yu Gyeom in lane eight
is Cho Jae Jin's son.

748
00:48:57,493 --> 00:49:01,939
But he's not as fast as I expected.

749
00:49:01,939 --> 00:49:04,441
Of course, we'll have to see how the race ends.

750
00:49:04,441 --> 00:49:09,868
For now, Im Jeong Uk in lane three
is maintaining the lead.

751
00:49:11,648 --> 00:49:14,451
We were eighteen back then.

752
00:49:14,451 --> 00:49:19,311
Cho Yu Gyeom in lane eight
is now making the 100m turn.

753
00:49:20,166 --> 00:49:21,750
He's speeding up but needs more.

754
00:49:21,750 --> 00:49:25,264
He needs to push harder
to reach the lead group.

755
00:49:27,092 --> 00:49:31,511
Why is the boy I told you to bring
appearing on television?

756
00:49:36,025 --> 00:49:39,456
At that age, I couldn't do much,
even when angry at the world.

757
00:49:50,991 --> 00:49:54,888
An age where love only led to goodbyes.

758
00:49:54,888 --> 00:49:56,256
Eighteen.

759
00:50:08,595 --> 00:50:09,625
Stay calm.

760
00:50:09,625 --> 00:50:15,251
He's slowly moving up after the turn
and is now in fourth place.

761
00:50:15,251 --> 00:50:19,503
After the 100m turn, there are only
three athletes ahead of him.

762
00:50:19,503 --> 00:50:23,279
He's just made the 150m turn.

763
00:50:23,279 --> 00:50:26,932
Cho Yu Gyeom in lane eight.
He's starting to pull ahead!

764
00:50:26,932 --> 00:50:32,197
Cho Yu Gyeom is incredible.
He's starting his final spurt.

765
00:50:32,197 --> 00:50:35,991
Only Im Jeong Uk in lane three
is left in front of him now.

766
00:50:52,985 --> 00:50:56,850
Nevertheless, I wanted to try.

767
00:51:35,259 --> 00:51:38,929
[Cho Yu Gyeom, Upo High School, 1st Place]

768
00:51:38,929 --> 00:51:43,925
Cho Yu Gyeom in lane eight finishes
with a time of 1:48.08.

769
00:51:43,925 --> 00:51:49,315
That's amazing! This is the fastest time
we have seen in these preliminaries!

770
00:51:49,315 --> 00:51:53,238
It's even faster than the record
of the current ace, Baek Seung Woo.

771
00:51:53,238 --> 00:51:56,238
- Cho Yu Gyeom has taken first place.
- Yes.

772
00:51:56,238 --> 00:51:58,420
Where has this athlete been all this time?

773
00:51:58,420 --> 00:52:01,160
Incredible. First place, Cho Yu Gyeom, 1:48.08.

774
00:52:01,160 --> 00:52:04,621
- Second place, Im Jeong Uk, 1:49.38.
- Yes.

775
00:52:04,621 --> 00:52:06,565
It was an incredibly close race.

776
00:52:06,565 --> 00:52:11,597
Cho Yu Gyeom makes a brilliant comeback
from last to first place.

777
00:52:26,021 --> 00:52:27,835
Yes, Principal.

778
00:52:28,857 --> 00:52:30,359
What?

779
00:52:30,359 --> 00:52:34,906
I didn't submit it.
Yu Gyeom applied on his own.

780
00:52:37,704 --> 00:52:41,750
I heard Yu Gyeom explained it well...

781
00:52:43,411 --> 00:52:49,023
Yes. Anyway, I'll see you when I get back. Yes.

782
00:52:53,411 --> 00:52:54,755
Sir! Hurry up!

783
00:52:54,755 --> 00:52:57,145
- Sir! Meat! Meat!
- Meat! Meat!

784
00:52:57,145 --> 00:53:00,848
- Meat!
- Beef!

785
00:53:00,848 --> 00:53:02,573
Fine, eat up.

786
00:53:03,673 --> 00:53:06,478
- Is it beef?
- Beef?

787
00:53:06,478 --> 00:53:07,953
It's pork.

788
00:53:10,479 --> 00:53:12,933
- Pork it is! Pork!
- Pork! Pork!

789
00:53:12,933 --> 00:53:15,237
Don't you guys eat greens?

790
00:53:15,237 --> 00:53:17,611
- No way.
- No.

791
00:53:17,611 --> 00:53:19,738
- But why isn't Cho Yu Gyeom coming out?
- Yu Gyeom?

792
00:53:19,738 --> 00:53:21,393
- Right?
- Where did Yu Gyeom go?

793
00:53:21,393 --> 00:53:23,866
Sae Ryeong, why isn't Yu Gyeom out yet?

794
00:53:24,983 --> 00:53:26,248
Cho Yu Gyeom.

795
00:53:26,248 --> 00:53:28,460
- Cho Yu Gyeom!
- Cho Yu Gyeom!

796
00:53:30,082 --> 00:53:31,334
Congrats on first place.

797
00:53:31,334 --> 00:53:34,360
- Cho Yu Gyeom! Cho Yu Gyeom!
- My boyfriend rocks.

798
00:53:40,137 --> 00:53:41,214
What?

799
00:53:48,053 --> 00:53:50,348
Cho Yu Gyeom, what's going on?

800
00:53:50,348 --> 00:53:51,971
I think I have to go.

801
00:53:51,971 --> 00:53:53,291
Where?

802
00:53:54,116 --> 00:53:55,500
Where?

803
00:53:56,710 --> 00:53:58,375
Tell me where you're going.

804
00:53:59,752 --> 00:54:00,975
You know.

805
00:54:02,448 --> 00:54:04,512
- What?
- Take this.

806
00:54:04,512 --> 00:54:06,190
- What?
- Hey!

807
00:54:06,190 --> 00:54:07,554
Sir, where is he going?

808
00:54:07,554 --> 00:54:10,173
Who cares where he goes?

809
00:54:10,173 --> 00:54:13,294
I'm busy worrying about
the principal chewing me out.

810
00:54:14,746 --> 00:54:15,973
Sae Ryeong.

811
00:54:15,973 --> 00:54:18,015
Where did he say he was going?

812
00:54:33,479 --> 00:54:35,856
There's less than two weeks left.

813
00:54:35,856 --> 00:54:37,535
What are you talking about?

814
00:54:37,535 --> 00:54:38,947
Summer vacation.

815
00:54:39,847 --> 00:54:41,208
What about it?

816
00:54:42,337 --> 00:54:45,208
You said you'd be with Yu Gyeom
for the rest of your life.

817
00:54:45,208 --> 00:54:47,471
You're finally admitting it.

818
00:54:47,471 --> 00:54:48,638
Why?

819
00:54:48,638 --> 00:54:50,561
Did reality hit you that hard?

820
00:54:51,667 --> 00:54:55,589
Just two weeks out of your lifetime.

821
00:54:55,589 --> 00:54:58,343
I'm going to be with Yu Gyeom
just for that long.

822
00:54:58,343 --> 00:54:59,381
What?

823
00:55:00,551 --> 00:55:03,313
I was just going to give up and leave.

824
00:55:04,575 --> 00:55:05,819
No.

825
00:55:06,788 --> 00:55:08,369
I can't.

826
00:55:08,369 --> 00:55:11,107
It feels unfair no matter how I look at it.

827
00:55:11,107 --> 00:55:14,409
Look, no matter what you say,
Yu Gyeom already--

828
00:55:14,409 --> 00:55:15,630
No.

829
00:55:16,449 --> 00:55:18,075
You know it too.

830
00:55:19,410 --> 00:55:21,553
Cho Yu Gyeom still likes me.

831
00:55:21,553 --> 00:55:22,676
What?

832
00:55:23,867 --> 00:55:26,499
It's your loss if you end it like this.

833
00:55:26,499 --> 00:55:31,051
You have to date and break up properly
to have no regrets, right?

834
00:55:31,642 --> 00:55:34,146
If you don't send Yu Gyeom to me now...

835
00:55:35,544 --> 00:55:38,923
He'll spend his whole life
missing me by your side.

836
00:55:41,049 --> 00:55:42,830
Are you okay with that?

837
00:55:47,944 --> 00:55:49,083
Hey.

838
00:55:50,048 --> 00:55:51,881
Where do you get this confidence?

839
00:55:51,881 --> 00:55:53,271
Two weeks is all I need.

840
00:55:54,845 --> 00:55:56,210
Just two weeks.

841
00:55:57,668 --> 00:55:59,991
After that, he'll forget me.

842
00:56:01,221 --> 00:56:02,886
I'll forget him, too.

843
00:56:04,864 --> 00:56:07,766
And Yu Gyeom will stay by your side
for the rest of his life.

844
00:56:09,745 --> 00:56:11,789
I came here to tell you this.

845
00:56:12,791 --> 00:56:16,290
If I just take him, you might hold onto him
with self-harm.

846
00:56:16,290 --> 00:56:17,662
Kim Ha Yeon.

847
00:56:20,480 --> 00:56:21,902
I...

848
00:56:24,534 --> 00:56:27,055
I think you have changed a little.

849
00:56:28,176 --> 00:56:30,722
Just as I have changed over this summer.

850
00:56:30,722 --> 00:56:31,843
Hey.

851
00:57:17,271 --> 00:57:18,684
Ha Yeon.

852
00:57:25,821 --> 00:57:27,262
Yu Gyeom.

853
00:57:29,113 --> 00:57:30,460
Go ahead.

854
00:57:34,037 --> 00:57:36,963
I'm not going home tonight.

855
00:57:40,002 --> 00:57:41,104
Okay.

856
00:57:42,012 --> 00:57:43,397
Let's do that.

857
00:57:47,634 --> 00:57:53,158
Meeting you, holding your hand,
touching you, and hugging you.

858
00:57:54,580 --> 00:57:59,174
I dared to hope we would collide
as if everything would burn up.

859
00:58:01,004 --> 00:58:05,069
When I was eighteen, I could do nothing.
